WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
ASDRP / MOUSE VISUAL CORTEX
Can behavior help us predict the brain?
A visual-cortex encoding-model study using real mouse recordings.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
THE DATA
Two mice. Thousands of neurons.
Natural-image stimuli, pupil size, running speed, and neural responses.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
THE COMPARISON
Two models. One held-out test.
Stimulus only versus stimulus plus behavior, with training-only preprocessing.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
THE RESULT
0.126 → 0.158 | 0.154 → 0.203
Mean held-out correlation rises when behavior is added in both evaluated mice.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
THE ABLATION
Pupil improves both.
Running contributes differently across animals; the result is predictive, not causal.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
THE LIMIT
Two animals are not a population.
The next scientific step is replication beyond two animals with population-level uncertainty.

